box\\wcj-settings-meta-box-purchase-data.php','line'=>108,'source_sha256'=>'1392db4e1ca01768ec89261272aa2e603f20dac226284a12350d6fe0e713587c'))))),'tasks'=>array('toolbar'=>array('anchor'=>'booster-v10-s24-toolbar-category-links','label'=>'Show product categories in the WooCommerce toolbar','scope'=>'Applies to everyone allowed to manage WooCommerce. It only shows or hides category links; it does not change permissions or products.','blocked'=>'Needs the Admin Bar module and its WooCommerce menu option turned on. This task turns neither on.','states'=>array('Not set (default: Off)','Saved: Off','Saved: On','Existing value needs full settings'),'restore'=>'For seven days, Restore previous setting can undo your latest eligible save here while the setting and related options still match. It can restore Not set. If Booster cannot check your previous save, Restore is unavailable. You can make a new save, but it will not bring back that earlier change.','supported'=>'This shortcut checks whether it can work safely on your site before making a change. If it cannot continue, it shows a reason. The existing full settings remain available.','supported_details'=>'This guided task needs a qualified single-site, 64-bit installation with supported transactional storage, nonpersistent object caching, and verified WordPress, WooCommerce and Booster files. Updates or added integrations may disable this shortcut until requalified. Existing full settings remain available.'),'cost'=>array('anchor'=>'booster-v10-s24-fill-missing-costs','label'=>'Fill missing Booster product costs from legacy values','input'=>'Paste up to 20 simple product IDs. Repeated entries count toward the limit and are excluded.','scope'=>'Only the listed eligible products are considered. A blank or 0 Booster cost counts as already set and is not overwritten. Legacy values do not prove that a particular extension is installed.','consequence'=>'Changing current product costs can change displayed profit for older orders when Booster uses that calculation. The order records themselves are not edited.','execute_label'=>'Fill {eligible_count} product costs','preview_only'=>'Preview does not save costs. Check each eligible and excluded product before filling.','undo'=>'For seven days, Undo can clear unchanged costs created by your latest eligible fill while its settings and permissions still match. It does not restore other product data. A later editing attempt can make Undo unavailable even if the amount ends up the same.','prerequisite'=>'Needs Cost of Goods and its product-cost component turned on. The component is On by default when not saved. This task enables neither.','decimal'=>'Use nonnegative amounts with up to 9 digits before the decimal point and up to 6 after it. Use 0 or a nonzero first digit; no commas, leading zeroes, exponent notation or spaces. Other formats are kept unchanged, not treated as invalid prices.','calculation'=>'The filled field is one component. Calculated cost may also include extra expenses, custom fields and site filters.','limits'=>'Changes made directly in the database may not appear in the task\'s editing history. Undo still checks that the cost is unchanged before clearing it. An expired preview cannot fill more products; saved results and any eligible Undo remain available. If someone removes this cost field across the store, a product may still be protected by a recent fill. Undo will not delete a missing or changed cost. You can wait until that fill\'s seven-day recovery period ends, use the existing product editor, or contact support. Waiting applies only to a recent fill that Booster can still check, not to a past task it cannot check. If Booster cannot check your previous fill, its Undo is unavailable. You can start a new fill, but that does not bring back the earlier Undo. If Booster cannot check a product\'s earlier task, that product is left unchanged. Waiting will not fix this. Use the existing product editor for that product or contact support.','supported'=>'This shortcut checks whether it can work safely on your site before making a change. If it cannot continue, it shows a reason. The existing full settings remain available.','supported_details'=>'This guided task needs a qualified single-site, 64-bit installation with supported transactional storage, nonpersistent object caching, and verified WordPress, WooCommerce and Booster files. Updates or added integrations may disable this shortcut until requalified. Existing full settings remain available.')));
